      "worked_solution": "The notation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/e15c0b105ea984c36aeb1eae6f4e743fd66d4a152acf6f2fdc5a9f977760e39f.svg) means that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) approaches ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) *from the right*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/99421620750831182ef45a4cfda34ee4b36f772f88df5572783bffc3ea9580c5.png)\n\nFrom the given graph, we see that as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) approaches ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) from the right, the values of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) increase, approaching ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/b7dcbb40b0c8f515a6b1ee8773cbf301ab1f40446114fd0e5436b57fd08e3697.svg)\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/333a8ffca9eb9ad90f40e6a0a28a8119936d27bc840b0495c6b98eafec91d875.svg) as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/57038ceb8b89a8ded3292cf53d2875f5da509c824f4ad1cacd8ce1616f1cfff5.svg) So, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
